WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.028
Some tasks are high-risk because one person
could use them to take over an identity,

2
00:00:05.028 --> 00:00:09.200
break its link to the source of truth,
or open an app to the wrong people.

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.283
For those, the book requires two approvers
besides the person doing the work,

4
00:00:14.283 --> 00:00:17.187
both recorded before
any role is activated.

5
00:00:17.187 --> 00:00:20.866
The second approver checks that
the requester was verified,

6
00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:24.250
the change is exactly specified,
and the urgency is real.

7
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:29.141
ImmutableID repair is the telling
example: it left the help desk entirely,

8
00:00:29.141 --> 00:00:33.550
because the right fix is usually in
Active Directory, not the cloud.

9
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.900
And three detection rules
watch everything the desk does.

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:37.970
That's Part 1.
